>> title: Ginger-Garlic Paste
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: indian, ginger, garlic, base, condiment
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: adrak lehsun paste, ginger garlic paste, adrak lasun, GG paste
>> pairs-with: onion-tomato-masala
>> servings: 1 cup
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — raw garlic under oil is where botulism grows, so it is a fridge item with a two-week life and the oil is no preservative

>> step: peel and blitz to a rough paste
Blitz @fresh ginger{4%oz}(115 g; peel it by scraping with a teaspoon) and @garlic{4%oz}(115 g; peeled) in a #small food processor{} to a rough paste.

>> step: work in, blitz smooth
Work @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @neutral oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)paste{} and blitz smooth.

>> step: pack down, film with oil, into the fridge
Pack @&(~1)paste{} into a clean #jar{}, film the top with @neutral oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and put it in the fridge.
